      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not apply heavy cream or vegetable oil, as they trap heat and bacteria, which will make the burn worse and increase the risk of infection. The only safe thing to do right now is keep running cool water over the area for another 15-20 minutes until the pain subsides. If you absolutely must cover it temporarily, use a sterile, non-stick gauze pad held loosely with a clean cloth, but avoid any creams or oils until you can get proper medical care.",
